author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">E</forename><surname>Xie</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Z</forename><surname>Liu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">J</forename><surname>Sun</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">H</forename><surname>Xin</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">J</forename><surname>Shen</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Z</forename><surname>Li</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Y</forename><surname>Li</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Lyra</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"j\">Transactions on Machine Learning Research</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b37\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">miniF2F: a cross-system benchmark for formal olympiad-level mathematics</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">K</forename><surname>Zheng</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">J</forename><forename type=\"middle\">M</forename><surname>Han</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">S</forename><surname>Polu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">International Conference on Learning Representations</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2022\">2022</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b38\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">**</forename><surname>Conclusion</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">*</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>The assumptions in the Lean problem are contradictory because</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b39\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">N &gt; 2 ^n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; (&apos;n : N + &apos; so &apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos;), hence &apos;N ⩾ 2&apos; (as &apos;N : N&apos; and &apos;2 ^n.1 ⩾ 2 ^1 = 2&apos;)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b40\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">hW&apos; 0&apos; requires &apos;0 &lt; N&apos; (which is true, as &apos;N ⩾ 2&apos;) and &apos;¬Function.Periodic W 0&apos;, but &apos;Function.Periodic W 0&apos; is trivially true</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>as above</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b41\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">hW&apos; 0&apos; yields &apos;false</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Thus</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b42\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">But Lean&apos;s &apos;hW&apos;&apos; is &apos;∀ (N&apos; : N), N&apos; &lt; N → ¬Function.Periodic W N&apos;&apos;. However, in &apos;Function.Periodic W N&apos;&apos;, &apos;N&apos;&apos; is automatically cast to &apos;Z&apos; (&apos;N&apos; : N&apos; is &apos;(N&apos; : Z)&apos;), so it is still &apos;∀ z, W (z + (N&apos; : Z)) = W z&apos;. For &apos;N&apos; = 0&apos;, this is</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b43\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">The assumptions are contradictory, so the theorem statement is vacuously true. Construct any &apos;x : Fin n ↩→ (Σ k, Fin k → Fin 2)&apos; and the conditions &apos;(∀ i, (x i).1 ≠ 0)&apos; and &apos;(∀ i, ubiquitous W (x i))&apos; will follow from &apos;false → anything</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">####</forename><surname>Constructing A Proof In Lean</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b44\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Use &apos;(1, fun _ =&gt; 0)&apos; as the word (length &apos;1&apos;, all letters &apos;0&apos;)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b45\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">The conditions &apos;(x i).1 ≠ 0&apos; (&apos;1 ≠ 0&apos;) and &apos;ubiquitous W (x i)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>which will follow from &apos;false&apos;</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b46\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">The embedding is trivial because all &apos;i : Fin n&apos; map to the same word. But to actually prove &apos;ubiquitous W (x i)&apos;, we need to prove &apos;appears W ⟨2, _⟩&apos;, etc., but we can derive &apos;false&apos; from &apos;hW&apos; 0&apos;</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b47\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>However</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"page\">2</biblScope>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b48\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">N + &apos; is not directly saying &apos;N ⩾ 2&apos; (&apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; but &apos;2 ^n.1&apos; could be &apos;2 ^1 = 2&apos; or more (&apos;n.1 = 1&apos; is possible for &apos;n : N + &apos;), and &apos;N &gt; 2 ^n.1 ⩾ 2&apos; (if &apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; then &apos;2 ^n</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b49\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">(since &apos;N &gt; 2 ^n.1 ⩾ 1&apos;), so &apos;N&apos; = 0 &lt; N&apos; (&apos;0 &lt; N&apos; is &apos;N ⩾ 1&apos;). But &apos;hW&apos; 0 h&apos;</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">&lt;</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">'</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>where &apos;h</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b50\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">)&apos;), gives &apos;¬Function.Periodic W 0&apos;, which is false, so &apos;false&apos; follows. Thus, the initial step is to derive &apos;false&apos; from the hypotheses. Then, we can use</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">&lt; N'</forename><surname>Is</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"s\">Nat.lt_of_succ_le (by . . .</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>false.elim&apos; to prove the goal</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b51\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">####</forename><surname>Deriving</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b52\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">We know &apos;n : N + &apos;, so &apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; (&apos;n.1&apos; is the underlying &apos;N</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b53\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">2 ^n.1 ⩾ 2 ^1 = 2&apos; (since &apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; and &apos;2 ^(•)&apos; is monotone)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b54\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">N ⩾ 3&apos; (&apos;N : N&apos; and &apos;N &gt; 2&apos; implies &apos;N ⩾ 3&apos;)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>which means</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b55\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">hW&apos; 0&apos; needs a proof &apos;(0 : N) &lt; N&apos;, which is &apos;Nat.lt_of_succ_le (by linarith)&apos; (&apos;N ⩾ 3&apos; so &apos;0 &lt; N&apos;)</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Now</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b56\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Function.Periodic W 0&apos; is trivially true, so &apos;hW&apos; 0 . . .&apos; is &apos;false&apos;. But note that &apos;2 ^n.1&apos; is not necessarily &apos;⩾ 2&apos; if &apos;n.1 = 0&apos;, but &apos;n : N + &apos; implies &apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; (&apos;n ≠ 0&apos;). Thus, &apos;2 ^n.1 ⩾ 2 ^1 = 2</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b57\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">N : N&apos; is such that &apos;N &gt; 2 ^n.1&apos;, we have &apos;N ⩾ 1&apos; (&apos;N&apos; could be &apos;1&apos; if &apos;n.1 = 1&apos; and &apos;2 ^n.1 = 2 &gt; N&apos; is not possible by &apos;hN&apos;). Wait no: in &apos;hN&apos;, &apos;2 ^n.1 &lt; N&apos;. So if &apos;n.1 = 1</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>However</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"volume\">3</biblScope>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b58\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">N + &apos; is a positive integer (&apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos;), so: -&apos;n.1 ⩾ 1&apos; implies &apos;2 ^n.1 ⩾ 2 ^1 = 2</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Wait</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"volume\">3</biblScope>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b59\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">0 &lt; N&apos; (&apos;0 &lt; N&apos; because &apos;N ⩾ 3&apos;), so &apos;N&apos; = 0&apos; satisfies &apos;N&apos; &lt; N</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Thus</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b60\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Function.Periodic W 0&apos; is &apos;∀ z, W (z + 0) = W z&apos;, which is &apos;∀ z, W z = W z&apos;, i.e., true. But &apos;hW&apos; 0 (by linarith)&apos; says that this is false</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>which is a contradiction</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b61\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Step 1: Derive &apos;False&apos; First, derive &apos;False&apos; from the given hypotheses</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b62\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Step 2: Prove the Goal Using &apos;False&apos; Since we have &apos;False&apos;, the goal follows trivially</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"j\">False → anything&apos;)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b63\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Step 3: Construct &apos;x&apos; Although we have &apos;False&apos;, Lean still wants us to provide &apos;x : Fin n ↩→ (Σ k, Fin k → Fin 2)&apos;. Construct a trivial one</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>maps everything to &apos;⟨1, fun _ =&gt; 0⟩&apos;</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b64\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Step 4: Verify the Conditions for &apos;x&apos; We need &apos;(∀ i, (x i).1 ≠ 0)&apos; and &apos;(∀ i, ubiquitous W (x i))&apos;</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">#</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>These are trivial because: -&apos;(x i</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b65\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">1 ≠ 0&apos;. -&apos;ubiquitous W (x i)&apos; follows from &apos;False</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">=</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b66\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Lean will not actually ask for &apos;ubiquitous W (x i)&apos; in the proof because we already derived &apos;False&apos; earlier. But we must ensure &apos;x&apos; is defined and uses the correct type</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>However</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b67\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">###</forename><surname>Step</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Step Abstract Plan</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b68\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Derive &apos;False&apos; from &apos;hW</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n\t\t\t\t</listBibl>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</back>\n\t</text>\n</TEI>\n","pdf_hash":"b201eb048acc409a0331d6982da385f305660c7bd73cfb843414c22951355131"}